# Passes the Metal saver draws differently from GL on purpose (ss-ss8).
# backendcheck.sh judges each of them, and all its fixtures, against its
# goldens (parity/golden/<pass>) instead of GL. One per line: the pass, then
# why. A pass goes in here in the pull request that changes its look.
stars    ss-ss8.2: no streak along a wrap (GL streaks a wrapping star for a frame); ss-ss8.3: 4x MSAA
tunnel   ss-ss8.2: true cos and sin (GL's rsCosf tables lose the argument past ~400); ss-ss8.3: 4x MSAA
sun      the stars pass with the sun in view: its stars, as stars
